1
00:02:08,378 --> 00:02:10,379
( Flutter of wings )

2
00:02:27,564 --> 00:02:29,148
( Sniffs )

3
00:02:30,692 --> 00:02:32,360
( Exhales )

4
00:03:19,199 --> 00:03:21,242
( Guard 's whistle )

5
00:03:28,125 --> 00:03:30,001
Come on , sir , give us a penny !

6
00:03:32,379 --> 00:03:33,254
Run !

7
00:03:34,423 --> 00:03:35,923
Sorry .

8
00:03:45,475 --> 00:03:48,436
Lucky heather , sir ? Come on , sir .

9
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:50,479
Looking for someone ?

10
00:03:50,564 --> 00:03:53,608
Er ... Yes , actually , I ...

11
00:03:53,692 --> 00:03:56,611
Mr. Gray . Welcome to London , sir .

12
00:04:06,330 --> 00:04:08,331
DRIVER : Go on , lady . Off you go !

13
00:04:35,359 --> 00:04:36,776
Whoa .

14
00:04:38,987 --> 00:04:41,656
And here we are , sir . Welcome home .

15
00:04:49,957 --> 00:04:52,667
I hope you 'll find everything to your liking , sir .

16
00:04:52,751 --> 00:04:54,752
Nothing 's changed since I was a boy .

17
00:04:54,836 --> 00:04:56,420
Sir .

18
00:05:11,937 --> 00:05:13,813
I 'm sorry for your loss , sir .

19
00:05:13,897 --> 00:05:15,731
May I prepare some tea ?

20
00:05:15,816 --> 00:05:17,817
Thank you , Victor .

21
00:05:27,577 --> 00:05:29,328
( Creaking )

22
00:06:07,617 --> 00:06:10,244
( Melancholy melody )

23
00:06:31,558 --> 00:06:35,561
I 've no doubt London will hold many new friends and adventures for you .

24
00:06:35,645 --> 00:06:37,855
- I hope so . - So do I.

25
00:06:37,939 --> 00:06:41,233
Oh ! This is somebody you simply must meet .

26
00:06:41,318 --> 00:06:43,736
This is one of our finest artists , Basil Hallward .

27
00:06:43,820 --> 00:06:46,530
Agatha , please , a humble student of beauty .

28
00:06:49,576 --> 00:06:51,035
- What do you think ? - Oh .

29
00:06:52,954 --> 00:06:55,164
AGATHA : That 's quite a likeness .

30
00:07:28,240 --> 00:07:30,658
- Basil . - Hmm ?

31
00:07:30,742 --> 00:07:32,451
I 've been in London two weeks now .

32
00:07:32,536 --> 00:07:35,121
The only people I 've met are Agatha 's charitable group .

33
00:07:35,205 --> 00:07:37,081
Well , you 've met me .

34
00:07:37,165 --> 00:07:38,874
Of course .

35
00:07:39,918 --> 00:07:41,460
I didn 't mean ...

36
00:07:41,545 --> 00:07:44,171
These parties are terribly dull , Dorian .

37
00:07:44,256 --> 00:07:47,383
- You won 't be missing anything . - I 'm sure you 're right .

38
00:07:47,467 --> 00:07:48,759
I just ...

39
00:07:50,178 --> 00:07:52,221
.. thought it might be fun .

40
00:07:58,520 --> 00:08:00,604
( String quartet plays )

41
00:08:10,574 --> 00:08:12,283
MAN : Oh ...

42
00:08:12,367 --> 00:08:14,368
Dear me , no .

43
00:08:14,452 --> 00:08:15,953
Shabby .

44
00:08:16,997 --> 00:08:18,914
Wife , drink .

45
00:08:23,795 --> 00:08:26,130
There . I 'll fetch us some drinks .

46
00:08:26,214 --> 00:08:30,259
WOMAN : Find her a good husband who knows how to behave to a woman .

47
00:08:30,343 --> 00:08:33,012
The only way to behave is to make love to her if she 's pretty

48
00:08:33,096 --> 00:08:35,472
and to someone else if she 's plain . Excuse me .

49
00:08:36,308 --> 00:08:38,142
( Laughter )

50
00:08:39,477 --> 00:08:40,853
Cigarette ?

51
00:08:41,980 --> 00:08:43,939
No , thank you .

52
00:08:44,816 --> 00:08:47,026
I find a cigarette to be the perfect pleasure .

53
00:08:47,110 --> 00:08:49,195
It is exquisite

54
00:08:49,279 --> 00:08:51,280
and leaves one unsatisfied .

55
00:08:57,329 --> 00:08:59,330
( Women laugh )

56
00:09:03,335 --> 00:09:05,294
You 're Kelso 's grandson .

57
00:09:05,378 --> 00:09:06,629
Yes .

58
00:09:07,881 --> 00:09:09,840
- Did you know him ? - I met him once .

59
00:09:09,925 --> 00:09:12,009
It was enough to give a cheer last month

60
00:09:12,093 --> 00:09:14,094
when he rasped his last sour breath .

61
00:09:15,472 --> 00:09:18,891
One assumes you inherited the withered old goat 's estate ?

62
00:09:20,185 --> 00:09:22,228
Being a little orphan isn 't all bad .

63
00:09:23,521 --> 00:09:27,066
" An earnest young man with a beautiful nature , " according to Agatha .

64
00:09:27,150 --> 00:09:31,403
I 'd pictured some freckled country oaf in ghastly dress .

65
00:09:33,698 --> 00:09:35,783
I see I was only half right .

66
00:09:37,744 --> 00:09:39,536
It could be worse .

67
00:09:39,621 --> 00:09:43,290
Gladys Allonby 's been dressed for her 14th birthday ever since her 40th .

68
00:09:44,125 --> 00:09:47,169
If Radley spent less time in church and more at his tailor 's ,

69
00:09:47,254 --> 00:09:49,630
he might not so resemble a badly-bound hymn book .

70
00:09:50,715 --> 00:09:53,217
Are you sure you won 't take a cigarette ?

71
00:09:53,218 --> 00:09:55,803
I get them directly from Cairo .

72
00:09:55,887 --> 00:09:58,931
I see you 've met our charming host .

73
00:10:00,517 --> 00:10:01,809
Hm ?

74
00:10:01,893 --> 00:10:03,894
Pay no attention to anything he tells you .

75
00:10:03,979 --> 00:10:05,980
How rude . Henry Wotton .

76
00:10:06,064 --> 00:10:07,523
Victoria , my wife .

77
00:10:08,608 --> 00:10:10,484
My aunt , alas , you know .

78
00:10:10,568 --> 00:10:14,113
Oh , I 'm so glad you 've met . You might learn some manners from this boy .

79
00:10:14,197 --> 00:10:16,240
I 've found some more guests for you to insult .

80
00:10:16,324 --> 00:10:18,534
I knew I kept her for something .

81
00:10:19,494 --> 00:10:22,621
I do hope our paths cross again , Mr. Gray .

82
00:10:24,124 --> 00:10:27,167
Thank you for the cigarette ... ( Coughs ) .. cigarette .

83
00:10:27,252 --> 00:10:29,211
An acquired taste .

84
00:10:29,296 --> 00:10:32,214
- No , it 's actually quite pleasant . - No , I meant Henry .

85
00:10:32,299 --> 00:10:33,674
( Giggles )

86
00:10:35,010 --> 00:10:37,553
There 's some people I want you to meet .

87
00:10:48,023 --> 00:10:50,441
( Gas lamp sputters )

88
00:11:13,173 --> 00:11:15,174
( Rumble of thunder )

89
00:11:21,723 --> 00:11:23,724
( Sputtering continues )

90
00:11:37,030 --> 00:11:39,031
( Gas lamp sputters )

91
00:12:01,388 --> 00:12:03,389
MAN : Dorian ... - ( Bolt clanks back )

92
00:12:03,473 --> 00:12:05,265
( Whimpers )

93
00:12:21,783 --> 00:12:23,992
( Rats squeak and scamper )

94
00:12:27,288 --> 00:12:29,289
( Fluttering )

95
00:12:30,333 --> 00:12:32,334
( Rats scampering )

96
00:12:34,712 --> 00:12:36,713
( Rats squeak )

97
00:12:40,301 --> 00:12:41,927
( Clink )

98
00:13:01,114 --> 00:13:03,699
DORIAN : Aren 't you tired of looking at me yet ?

99
00:13:03,783 --> 00:13:05,701
BASIL : Certainly not .

100
00:13:05,785 --> 00:13:07,494
The more I look ...

101
00:13:09,247 --> 00:13:11,415
.. the more I see .

102
00:13:34,606 --> 00:13:38,317
It must be nearly finished , man . It isn 't the Sistine Chapel .

103
00:13:38,401 --> 00:13:41,403
Do you remember when I told you you could sit in if you were quiet ?

104
00:13:41,488 --> 00:13:44,072
- I want to see it . - No , no , don 't .

105
00:13:44,157 --> 00:13:46,783
He won 't even let me have a peek .

106
00:13:52,290 --> 00:13:55,542
Agatha tells me your father was also an artist .

107
00:13:55,627 --> 00:13:58,253
- Apparently so . - Kelso must have been delighted ,

108
00:13:58,254 --> 00:14:01,131
his daughter falling for some penniless painter .

109
00:14:01,341 --> 00:14:03,258
( Laughs )

110
00:14:03,343 --> 00:14:05,385
No wonder they eloped .

111
00:14:05,470 --> 00:14:07,846
- I never knew my parents . - Of course .

112
00:14:07,931 --> 00:14:09,890
Typhus is so awful .

113
00:14:09,974 --> 00:14:12,976
Your poor mother carried off in childbirth .

114
00:14:15,146 --> 00:14:17,814
Do you take such interest in everyone you meet ?

115
00:14:17,899 --> 00:14:19,942
Not everyone I meet is so interesting .

116
00:14:20,026 --> 00:14:23,028
Henry , why don 't you go for a stroll ,

117
00:14:23,112 --> 00:14:25,489
while I just work up the background ?

118
00:14:25,573 --> 00:14:27,533
You don 't need Dorian for that .

119
00:14:28,284 --> 00:14:29,868
Let 's both take a break .

120
00:14:29,953 --> 00:14:34,248
- Perhaps we should all get some air . - Yes , and I know just the place .

121
00:14:47,887 --> 00:14:52,474
MAN : Look . It 's rancid ! It 's rancid ! It 's only five days old . I 'm not paying .

122
00:14:52,559 --> 00:14:54,560
( Shouting and screaming )

123
00:14:56,896 --> 00:14:58,855
Come on , Dorian .

124
00:14:59,857 --> 00:15:00,899
Sorry .

125
00:15:00,984 --> 00:15:03,277
You see why Agatha is so keen to help Whitechapel ?

126
00:15:03,361 --> 00:15:06,071
Don 't you think we should at least try to make a difference ?

127
00:15:06,155 --> 00:15:10,492
I 've no desire to change anything in England , except the weather .

128
00:15:15,039 --> 00:15:16,999
( Fiddle music )

129
00:15:17,083 --> 00:15:19,585
Welcome to my little Hellfire Club .

130
00:15:24,799 --> 00:15:28,176
- Here you are , gents . - In one .

131
00:15:28,261 --> 00:15:29,720
No , don 't , don 't .

132
00:15:32,098 --> 00:15:34,182
- ( Coughs ) - Barkeeper .

133
00:15:34,183 --> 00:15:36,059
Again .

134
00:15:37,103 --> 00:15:40,647
How say you and the handsome young man stuff me double ?

135
00:15:40,732 --> 00:15:43,984
Er , no , thank you . We nonetheless wish you godspeed

136
00:15:44,068 --> 00:15:46,194
on your evening 's quest for romance .

137
00:15:47,488 --> 00:15:49,448
MAN : A little wider , my dear .

138
00:15:50,867 --> 00:15:52,743
Oh ! ( Giggles )

139
00:15:54,245 --> 00:15:57,456
Don 't worry . He 's a doctor .

140
00:15:59,626 --> 00:16:01,418
There 's no shame in pleasure , Mr. Gray .

141
00:16:01,502 --> 00:16:03,086
Man just wants to be happy .

142
00:16:03,171 --> 00:16:07,257
But society wants him to be good . And when he 's good , Man is rarely happy .

143
00:16:07,342 --> 00:16:09,635
But when he 's happy , he 's always good .

144
00:16:11,262 --> 00:16:14,431
You do want to be good , don 't you , Mr. Gray , and happy ?

145
00:16:14,515 --> 00:16:17,726
Isn 't there a price to pay for that sort of business ?

146
00:16:17,810 --> 00:16:19,853
She 's quite affordable .

147
00:16:20,563 --> 00:16:23,774
But what I was asking was about the effect on ...

148
00:16:23,858 --> 00:16:25,484
Buy a lady a drink ?

149
00:16:25,568 --> 00:16:28,570
- On what ? - Well , on one 's soul .

150
00:16:30,156 --> 00:16:31,990
One 's soul ?

151
00:16:32,909 --> 00:16:34,660
This is my church .

152
00:16:36,204 --> 00:16:40,248
With this dram , right now , I nail my soul to the Devil 's altar .

153
00:16:40,333 --> 00:16:45,045
You 'll never meet a more eloquent philosopher of pure folly .

154
00:16:47,048 --> 00:16:50,467
Come on , Dorian . It 's time we showed you what we 've made .

155
00:16:50,551 --> 00:16:53,845
- Really ? - The boy hasn 't finished his gin .

156
00:16:53,930 --> 00:16:57,432
Go and fiddle with your background . We 'll be along shortly .

157
00:16:57,517 --> 00:16:59,393
( Drunken singing )

158
00:16:59,477 --> 00:17:01,395
BASIL : Your picture awaits you , Dorian .

159
00:17:11,572 --> 00:17:14,282
Perhaps you should go and speak to her .

160
00:17:15,827 --> 00:17:17,452
I didn 't realize she ...

161
00:17:17,537 --> 00:17:19,621
Don 't be timid . Go .

162
00:17:21,666 --> 00:17:24,418
- I wouldn 't know where to ... - You see , I envy you .

163
00:17:24,502 --> 00:17:25,919
Me ?

164
00:17:26,003 --> 00:17:27,421
Everything 's possible for you

165
00:17:27,505 --> 00:17:30,006
because you have the only two things worth having .

166
00:17:30,091 --> 00:17:31,550
Youth ...

167
00:17:31,634 --> 00:17:33,427
and beauty .

168
00:17:36,180 --> 00:17:37,806
Come on , let 's go .

169
00:17:37,890 --> 00:17:39,891
The moment 's lost .

170
00:17:44,105 --> 00:17:46,106
That was probably her husband .

171
00:17:46,190 --> 00:17:48,191
Yes , very sensible .

172
00:17:49,360 --> 00:17:51,987
People die of common sense , Dorian ,

173
00:17:52,071 --> 00:17:54,865
one lost moment at a time .

174
00:17:54,949 --> 00:17:57,033
Life is a moment . There is no hereafter .

175
00:17:59,245 --> 00:18:01,913
So make it burn always

176
00:18:01,998 --> 00:18:04,040
with the hardest flame .

177
00:18:13,926 --> 00:18:15,927
HENRY : Well , Basil ...

178
00:18:17,096 --> 00:18:19,389
.. it 's quite the best thing you 've done .

179
00:18:21,476 --> 00:18:23,310
You 'll be the talk of the town .

180
00:18:24,562 --> 00:18:26,646
Both of you .

181
00:18:29,442 --> 00:18:31,735
Speak up , boy . You 'll hurt his feelings .

182
00:18:34,906 --> 00:18:36,865
Is that really how I look ?

183
00:18:36,949 --> 00:18:39,034
It 's just so ...

184
00:18:40,036 --> 00:18:41,411
.. life-like .

185
00:18:41,496 --> 00:18:43,622
HENRY : Better than life .

186
00:18:46,834 --> 00:18:48,835
He 'll always look like that .

187
00:18:50,630 --> 00:18:53,799
You , Mr. Gray , I 'm afraid will not .

188
00:18:55,885 --> 00:18:59,763
In time , Mother Nature will come a very poor second to Father Basil .

189
00:18:59,847 --> 00:19:03,308
- Some things are precious for not lasting . - Poppycock .

190
00:19:03,392 --> 00:19:06,978
We wither and scar because the gods are cruel and hateful .

191
00:19:09,732 --> 00:19:12,776
Perhaps I should nail my soul to the Devil 's altar .

192
00:19:13,486 --> 00:19:15,362
And remain as you are ? Fair trade .

193
00:19:15,446 --> 00:19:17,614
How about another gin instead ?

194
00:19:18,491 --> 00:19:21,201
All that hocus-pocus , endless conjurations ,

195
00:19:21,285 --> 00:19:23,578
books bound in infant skin ,

196
00:19:23,579 --> 00:19:26,790
pentacles of fire , drinking the blood of virgins .

197
00:19:26,874 --> 00:19:30,544
Dorian wouldn 't really barter his soul .

198
00:19:32,880 --> 00:19:34,548
Would you , Dorian ?

199
00:19:37,301 --> 00:19:38,844
Would you ?

200
00:19:40,596 --> 00:19:42,347
Yes .

201
00:19:49,397 --> 00:19:51,398
( Gasps and applause )

202
00:19:53,234 --> 00:19:57,696
Oh , you really have captured something quite exquisite , Basil .

203
00:19:57,780 --> 00:20:00,073
I 've never known a subject so unaffected .

204
00:20:00,157 --> 00:20:04,536
The brush just seemed to dance and I just painted what I saw .

205
00:20:04,620 --> 00:20:06,621
Kelso will turn in his grave .

206
00:20:08,875 --> 00:20:11,167
He didn 't care to look at me .

207
00:20:11,252 --> 00:20:12,586
He blamed me for my mother ,

208
00:20:12,670 --> 00:20:14,713
for her death .

209
00:20:14,797 --> 00:20:17,299
There are no limits to the ugliness of old men .

210
00:20:17,884 --> 00:20:20,218
Lips ! And his eyes !

211
00:20:20,303 --> 00:20:22,762
Almost a match for the original .

212
00:20:22,847 --> 00:20:25,974
- You must get used to being looked at . - Well , it 's a fine painting .

213
00:20:26,058 --> 00:20:29,603
- I don 't mean the painting . - Mr. Gray , if you please .

214
00:20:33,566 --> 00:20:36,735
- That went rather well , didn 't it ? - A triumph , Mr. Gray .

215
00:20:37,445 --> 00:20:39,070
The first of many .

216
00:20:44,327 --> 00:20:46,828
May I say , sir ,

217
00:20:46,913 --> 00:20:49,289
your mother would be very proud to see you today .

218
00:20:53,669 --> 00:20:55,503
Shall I draw your bath ?

219
00:20:55,588 --> 00:20:57,422
It 's rather early .

220
00:21:00,051 --> 00:21:02,010
Do we have any gin ?

221
00:21:02,094 --> 00:21:04,095
I believe not , sir .

222
00:21:05,932 --> 00:21:08,975
Then perhaps you might summon me a hansom ?

223
00:21:17,109 --> 00:21:19,194
- Go on , poke him ! - I am poking him !

224
00:21:19,278 --> 00:21:21,279
Check his pockets !

225
00:21:22,198 --> 00:21:23,865
Oi !

226
00:21:23,950 --> 00:21:25,700
Yes ?

227
00:21:25,785 --> 00:21:28,036
- Wet your pizzle , sir ? - Hello , handsome .

228
00:21:28,120 --> 00:21:29,663
( Barks )

229
00:21:29,747 --> 00:21:31,665
( Woman laughs )

230
00:21:31,749 --> 00:21:33,750
( Man laughs drunkenly ) Boy !

231
00:21:38,214 --> 00:21:40,173
( Ship 's bell and cry of seagulls )

232
00:21:43,302 --> 00:21:45,720
Have a box , my lord ? Just a bob .

233
00:21:45,805 --> 00:21:47,806
You 've only missed a little .

234
00:21:52,895 --> 00:21:54,813
This young lady ...

235
00:21:54,897 --> 00:21:58,108
Miss Sibyl Vane , my lord , in the role of Ophelia .

236
00:21:58,192 --> 00:22:00,568
.. see that noble and most sovereign reason

237
00:22:00,653 --> 00:22:04,906
like sweet bells jangled , out of tune and harsh .

238
00:22:04,991 --> 00:22:08,660
That unmatch 'd form and feature of blown youth

239
00:22:08,744 --> 00:22:10,620
blasted with ecstasy .

240
00:22:11,789 --> 00:22:13,790
Oh , woe is me .

241
00:22:17,003 --> 00:22:18,586
( Door opens )

242
00:22:18,671 --> 00:22:20,839
MANAGER : May I present

243
00:22:20,923 --> 00:22:24,843
the Theatre Royale 's Miss Sibyl Vane , my lord ?

244
00:22:28,014 --> 00:22:29,639
( Door closes )

245
00:22:33,352 --> 00:22:35,311
I 'm not really a lord .

246
00:22:35,396 --> 00:22:37,605
I don 't know why he keeps saying that .

247
00:22:37,690 --> 00:22:40,108
We don 't get many gentlemen in this theatre .

248
00:22:40,192 --> 00:22:41,985
Really ?

249
00:22:42,069 --> 00:22:44,362
Well , then , I shall recommend it ...

250
00:22:45,489 --> 00:22:47,157
.. to them .

251
00:22:48,200 --> 00:22:50,035
( Clears throat )

252
00:22:53,956 --> 00:22:56,166
May I ask what brings you to my dressing room ?

253
00:22:56,250 --> 00:22:57,584
Well , I ...

254
00:22:57,668 --> 00:23:00,211
I just happened to be passing the theatre and ...

255
00:23:02,465 --> 00:23:05,300
- Well , you see , I was in the gin shop ... - I know .

256
00:23:06,427 --> 00:23:08,636
You remember ?

257
00:23:08,721 --> 00:23:12,015
Well , a friend took me there for the first time .

258
00:23:12,099 --> 00:23:15,310
Well , I say the first time . Of course , I have ...

259
00:23:17,772 --> 00:23:20,523
Well , I wanted to ... wanted to say hello ,

260
00:23:20,608 --> 00:23:23,026
but then you left with ...

261
00:23:23,110 --> 00:23:25,111
- With Jim . - Yes .

262
00:23:25,946 --> 00:23:27,489
Quite .

263
00:23:28,783 --> 00:23:30,492
Jim .

264
00:23:31,577 --> 00:23:33,661
My brother .

265
00:23:34,663 --> 00:23:36,539
Brother ?

266
00:23:36,624 --> 00:23:39,459
- Mm . - Well , that 's splendid !

267
00:23:44,173 --> 00:23:46,257
Sorry . It was wrong of me to ...

268
00:23:46,342 --> 00:23:49,552
Please forgive my intrusion , Miss Vane .

269
00:23:49,637 --> 00:23:53,348
Wait ! There 's something you haven 't told me .

270
00:23:58,270 --> 00:24:00,230
Yes , of course .

271
00:24:00,314 --> 00:24:02,315
I do beg your pardon .

272
00:24:05,986 --> 00:24:07,821
Ophelia is a most challenging role

273
00:24:07,905 --> 00:24:12,075
and your performance this evening was ... impeccable .

274
00:24:12,159 --> 00:24:14,077
In fact , extraordinary .

275
00:24:14,161 --> 00:24:15,495
In fact ...

276
00:24:16,747 --> 00:24:18,748
.. you are extraordinary .

277
00:24:20,376 --> 00:24:22,585
And when I saw you on the stage ,

278
00:24:22,670 --> 00:24:27,507
and even more so , now I stand before you ,

279
00:24:27,591 --> 00:24:32,095
I am awestruck and humbled by your radiance .

280
00:24:34,890 --> 00:24:36,975
I meant your name .

281
00:24:38,811 --> 00:24:40,812
You didn 't tell me your name .

282
00:24:44,733 --> 00:24:46,192
( Both laugh )

283
00:25:05,754 --> 00:25:08,965
So , how many other girls do you bring here ?

284
00:25:09,884 --> 00:25:11,134
Hundreds .

285
00:25:11,218 --> 00:25:13,011
Thousands .

286
00:25:13,095 --> 00:25:15,555
- You must be courting dozens at least . - No .

287
00:25:15,639 --> 00:25:17,390
You can tell me the truth .

288
00:25:17,474 --> 00:25:19,559
There 's only you .

289
00:25:22,897 --> 00:25:25,398
There 's only you .

290
00:25:34,783 --> 00:25:37,827
Tell me , what are your actual relations with this young thing ?

291
00:25:37,912 --> 00:25:42,415
- A fraction of respect , man . - It 's not like that . Sibyl 's sacred .

292
00:25:44,168 --> 00:25:47,003
It 's only the scared things that are worth touching .

293
00:25:47,087 --> 00:25:49,631
People nowadays fear their passions .

294
00:25:49,715 --> 00:25:51,841
- Well , I don 't . - Of course you do .

295
00:25:51,926 --> 00:25:54,761
We 're taught terror from the nursery .

296
00:25:54,845 --> 00:25:57,722
Terror of God ,

297
00:25:57,723 --> 00:25:59,098
or , even worse , of scandal .

298
00:25:59,183 --> 00:26:02,310
We 're taught to spend our entire lives cowering in self-denial .

299
00:26:04,063 --> 00:26:08,566
The truth , Mr. Gray , is that every impulse we strangle only poisons us .

300
00:26:08,651 --> 00:26:11,110
You 'll make him wish he 'd never mentioned the girl .

301
00:26:11,195 --> 00:26:13,154
Voilà , monsieur .

302
00:26:13,239 --> 00:26:15,240
There 's something missing .

303
00:26:24,416 --> 00:26:25,959
Thank you , Harry .

304
00:26:26,043 --> 00:26:28,336
I took the liberty of filling it with my blend .

305
00:26:38,264 --> 00:26:40,223
Oh , Dorian .

306
00:26:40,307 --> 00:26:42,558
- ( Dorian plays piano ) - It 's beautiful .

307
00:26:43,727 --> 00:26:46,312
I just thought it would suit you .

308
00:27:14,842 --> 00:27:17,927
I should be going . Jim will worry .

309
00:27:18,012 --> 00:27:19,512
Of course .

310
00:27:23,726 --> 00:27:25,518
Or we could ...

311
00:27:26,520 --> 00:27:28,146
I mean ...

312
00:27:29,023 --> 00:27:31,357
You could ...

313
00:27:32,359 --> 00:27:33,735
.. stay ...

314
00:27:34,695 --> 00:27:36,195
.. here ...

315
00:27:37,031 --> 00:27:39,032
.. with me .

316
00:27:40,909 --> 00:27:42,952
We shouldn 't be afraid of our feelings , Sib .

317
00:27:43,037 --> 00:27:44,329
It 's just ...

318
00:27:44,413 --> 00:27:46,247
I 've seen other girls

319
00:27:46,332 --> 00:27:49,834
who give themselves , and then I 've seen what becomes of them .

320
00:27:49,918 --> 00:27:51,377
I love you .

321
00:27:57,092 --> 00:28:00,386
Forgive me . I didn 't mean ...

322
00:28:05,392 --> 00:28:07,935
You 're all I ever want in the world .

323
00:28:41,261 --> 00:28:43,763
( Lock clunks )

324
00:28:48,852 --> 00:28:50,561
Boy !

325
00:28:55,651 --> 00:28:58,152
You might have a little scar there .

326
00:28:58,237 --> 00:29:00,279
Well , it won 't be a first .

327
00:29:02,241 --> 00:29:04,200
My back .

328
00:29:09,581 --> 00:29:10,998
What ?

329
00:29:20,801 --> 00:29:22,802
You 're perfect .

330
00:29:25,139 --> 00:29:27,140
- Engaged ? - It 's wonderful , isn 't it ?

331
00:29:27,224 --> 00:29:29,016
( Ladies murmur )

332
00:29:29,101 --> 00:29:31,269
I wanted you all to be the first to know .

333
00:29:31,478 --> 00:29:33,938
- Congratulations , Dorian . - Thank you .

334
00:29:34,356 --> 00:29:37,567
May I ask how you came to propose marriage ?

335
00:29:37,651 --> 00:29:40,153
I suppose I didn 't really make a formal proposal .

336
00:29:40,237 --> 00:29:44,449
I told her I loved her . She said it was her dream come true to be my wife .

337
00:29:46,869 --> 00:29:48,744
Women are wonderfully practical .

338
00:29:48,829 --> 00:29:50,037
( Laughter )

339
00:29:50,122 --> 00:29:52,415
Will you all come and see her perform tonight ?

340
00:29:54,501 --> 00:29:56,502
I 'm afraid I have an engagement .

341
00:29:57,337 --> 00:29:59,672
( Clears throat )

342
00:29:59,756 --> 00:30:01,716
And we 're due at the Burdons .

343
00:30:05,846 --> 00:30:09,599
Tell Burdon I 'll see him tomorrow . Why don 't you hail us a hansom ?

344
00:30:09,683 --> 00:30:12,143
- I love acting . - Goodbye , ladies .

345
00:30:12,144 --> 00:30:14,270
So much more real than life .

346
00:30:14,354 --> 00:30:16,856
I hope you 're pleased with yourself .

347
00:30:16,940 --> 00:30:18,900
Every experience is of value .

348
00:30:18,984 --> 00:30:21,777
And marriage is certainly an experience .

349
00:30:23,947 --> 00:30:26,741
Nobody is amused this time , Henry .

350
00:30:28,827 --> 00:30:30,870
I 'll talk to him .

351
00:30:33,457 --> 00:30:37,001
DORIAN : I got the sense the others don 't quite approve . Especially Basil .

352
00:30:37,085 --> 00:30:40,379
Perhaps Basil should be a little more fearless with his own feelings .

353
00:30:42,799 --> 00:30:45,885
I thought we might make a little stop en route to the theatre .

354
00:30:47,095 --> 00:30:48,888
I too have news .

355
00:30:50,140 --> 00:30:52,892
It seems my wife is with child .

356
00:30:52,976 --> 00:30:54,936
Oh , congratulations .

357
00:30:55,020 --> 00:30:57,605
Don 't be absurd . It 's the beginning of the end .

358
00:30:57,689 --> 00:30:59,190
So , indulge me .

359
00:31:04,988 --> 00:31:07,323
- Ah , Harry . - Alan .

360
00:31:07,407 --> 00:31:09,617
Firkytoodling at last , I see .

361
00:31:12,371 --> 00:31:15,748
- Come along , ladies . - It 's good to see you .

362
00:31:19,920 --> 00:31:21,837
How delightful .

363
00:31:21,922 --> 00:31:23,339
Hello .

364
00:31:25,592 --> 00:31:27,218
Drink up .

365
00:31:27,302 --> 00:31:31,013
It won 't be long before you 're anchored to the perambulator .

366
00:31:31,098 --> 00:31:32,890
I don 't think so .

367
00:31:32,975 --> 00:31:34,850
Our friend is to marry .

368
00:31:34,935 --> 00:31:38,563
Ah , but we haven 't had a chance to win your heart .

369
00:31:38,647 --> 00:31:40,773
HENRY : Oh , well .

370
00:31:40,857 --> 00:31:43,150
Farewell to youth .

371
00:31:46,863 --> 00:31:47,989
No .

372
00:31:51,368 --> 00:31:53,077
Watch your step .

373
00:31:57,791 --> 00:32:00,251
Does Victoria know you come here ?

374
00:32:00,335 --> 00:32:04,755
My dear boy , marriage makes a life of deception absolutely necessary .

375
00:32:09,177 --> 00:32:11,596
Well , perhaps I have a stronger conscience .

376
00:32:11,680 --> 00:32:14,599
Conscience is just a polite term for cowardice .

377
00:32:21,440 --> 00:32:24,650
No civilized man regrets a pleasure .

378
00:32:37,998 --> 00:32:39,790
You see ?

379
00:32:42,085 --> 00:32:45,087
The only way to get rid of a temptation is to yield to it .

380
00:32:56,433 --> 00:32:59,685
Be searching always for new sensations , Dorian .

381
00:33:03,315 --> 00:33:04,857
Come .

382
00:33:05,817 --> 00:33:07,777
Come upstairs .

383
00:33:07,861 --> 00:33:10,029
Forbid yourself nothing .

384
00:33:11,073 --> 00:33:12,323
Come .

385
00:33:12,407 --> 00:33:15,660
- Nobody at all need know . - Come with me .

386
00:33:49,695 --> 00:33:51,696
( Moans of ecstasy )

387
00:33:54,199 --> 00:33:56,158
HENRY : The pleasure is all mine .

388
00:33:56,243 --> 00:33:58,953
- I 've heard so much about you . - And I you .

389
00:33:59,037 --> 00:34:02,248
Did you enjoy the show ? I couldn 't see you in the audience .

390
00:34:02,332 --> 00:34:04,166
I 'm afraid we ran a little late .

391
00:34:04,251 --> 00:34:06,293
Oh , where were you ?

392
00:34:06,378 --> 00:34:08,129
At the club .

393
00:34:08,213 --> 00:34:11,298
The truth is , my dear , we were celebrating your wonderful news .

394
00:34:12,259 --> 00:34:14,051
Very many congratulations .

395
00:34:14,052 --> 00:34:16,679
And Harry is to be a father .

396
00:34:16,763 --> 00:34:18,222
How wonderful .

397
00:34:18,306 --> 00:34:20,057
- Indeed . - In one .

398
00:34:20,142 --> 00:34:22,226
I 'm sure you 're eager to start a family , too ?

399
00:34:22,310 --> 00:34:24,019
Very much .

400
00:34:24,104 --> 00:34:26,230
( Laughs )

401
00:34:28,442 --> 00:34:30,609
Well , not quite yet .

402
00:34:30,694 --> 00:34:32,945
- Good night . - Good night , Charlie .

403
00:34:33,029 --> 00:34:34,697
'Night .

404
00:34:36,491 --> 00:34:38,784
We 're a little young , don 't you think ?

405
00:34:38,869 --> 00:34:40,494
Are we ?

406
00:34:43,790 --> 00:34:45,791
Perhaps I should take my leave .

407
00:34:46,752 --> 00:34:48,711
- Good night . - Er ...

408
00:34:48,795 --> 00:34:51,046
See you tomorrow , Harry .

409
00:34:51,131 --> 00:34:52,631
I 'm sure .

410
00:35:02,517 --> 00:35:04,935
I don 't think we need to rush , that 's all .

411
00:35:05,020 --> 00:35:06,812
( Beats drum )

412
00:35:10,150 --> 00:35:12,151
You sound different .

413
00:35:13,195 --> 00:35:15,029
Not at all .

414
00:35:17,157 --> 00:35:19,158
Were you at the club all night ?

415
00:35:20,035 --> 00:35:21,202
Yes .

416
00:35:23,747 --> 00:35:25,748
He 's a better liar than you .

417
00:35:26,833 --> 00:35:28,042
What ?

418
00:35:30,253 --> 00:35:33,005
I was just saying everything is so soon .

419
00:35:33,089 --> 00:35:37,092
- I gave myself to you . I thought you loved me . - And I do !

420
00:35:37,177 --> 00:35:39,845
Then make me your wife , not one of your whores !

421
00:35:41,473 --> 00:35:44,183
I think perhaps I ought to go .

422
00:35:45,101 --> 00:35:47,102
Don 't let him do this , Dorian .

423
00:35:51,358 --> 00:35:54,318
- This has nothing to do with Harry . - You said you loved me !

424
00:35:54,402 --> 00:35:55,945
And I do ! I do !

425
00:35:56,029 --> 00:35:57,947
Dorian , please !

426
00:35:58,031 --> 00:36:01,408
Please , Dorian ! Please , I love you !

427
00:36:15,215 --> 00:36:17,216
( Door slams )

428
00:36:25,308 --> 00:36:27,309
( Fly buzzes )

429
00:37:03,430 --> 00:37:05,431
( Chatter and laughter )

430
00:37:06,892 --> 00:37:09,768
Oh , Henry ! Dorian !

431
00:37:10,896 --> 00:37:14,106
Tell me , how was last night 's performance ?

432
00:37:20,614 --> 00:37:22,573
I 'm sorry .

433
00:37:25,160 --> 00:37:27,369
Have a drink .

434
00:37:27,454 --> 00:37:30,289
I can introduce you to the artist later , if you like .

435
00:37:32,959 --> 00:37:34,960
Never marry , Mr. Gray .

436
00:37:36,004 --> 00:37:38,714
It 's the only way to keep all one 's illusions .

437
00:37:41,468 --> 00:37:44,762
Chin up , dear boy . You 've a face like a slapped nancy .

438
00:37:46,306 --> 00:37:48,307
You 'll love again .

439
00:37:49,225 --> 00:37:51,226
And again . Do you have your cigarettes ?

440
00:37:51,311 --> 00:37:52,978
Of course .

441
00:37:59,194 --> 00:38:01,487
Don 't fear it , Dorian .

442
00:38:02,822 --> 00:38:04,823
The world is yours .

443
00:38:06,117 --> 00:38:08,410
For a season .

444
00:38:11,706 --> 00:38:13,791
( Whispering )

445
00:38:24,469 --> 00:38:26,887
Hello , Victor . Could you fetch us a bottle of the ... ?

446
00:38:26,972 --> 00:38:28,597
Anything !

447
00:38:29,599 --> 00:38:32,142
- What 's the matter ? - You 've a visitor , sir .

448
00:38:32,227 --> 00:38:35,646
A Mr. Vane . He seems disturbed .

449
00:38:35,730 --> 00:38:37,648
We 'll wait in the library .

450
00:38:37,732 --> 00:38:39,733
Victor , how about that bottle ?

451
00:38:44,364 --> 00:38:46,490
( Laughter )

452
00:39:14,894 --> 00:39:16,687
To what do I owe the pleasure , Jim ?

453
00:39:23,194 --> 00:39:27,281
Can I er ... Can I get you something to drink ?

454
00:39:29,701 --> 00:39:32,286
I don 't want this in my house .

455
00:39:33,371 --> 00:39:36,498
What happened with Sibyl was very unfortunate .

456
00:39:36,583 --> 00:39:38,625
But this was a gift

457
00:39:38,710 --> 00:39:40,794
and she really should keep ...

458
00:39:42,630 --> 00:39:44,381
It 's filthy .

459
00:39:44,466 --> 00:39:46,925
She was wearing it when they pulled her from the river .

460
00:39:51,431 --> 00:39:53,849
Why on earth was she ... ?

461
00:39:59,189 --> 00:40:01,190
She ... she can 't ...

462
00:40:02,484 --> 00:40:04,485
She can 't ...

463
00:40:12,202 --> 00:40:15,954
I wanted you to know ... she loved you .

464
00:40:16,039 --> 00:40:18,165
She was going to have your child .

465
00:40:20,752 --> 00:40:22,628
And you killed her .

466
00:40:25,381 --> 00:40:27,424
Jim ! Jim !

467
00:40:45,985 --> 00:40:47,486
Get up !

468
00:40:47,570 --> 00:40:49,530
Are you all right , sir ?

469
00:40:49,614 --> 00:40:51,615
Let me ...

470
00:40:51,699 --> 00:40:54,660
- help you up . - Sibyl 's dead .

471
00:40:54,744 --> 00:40:57,663
- Now , now . - Good night , ladies .

472
00:40:57,747 --> 00:40:59,665
( Jim sobs and shouts )

473
00:40:59,666 --> 00:41:01,875
Get up . Get up !

474
00:41:04,087 --> 00:41:09,341
We can 't have maniacs threatening decent people in their own homes .

475
00:41:09,425 --> 00:41:12,344
Alan treats a number of such deranged cases at Broadmoor .

476
00:41:12,428 --> 00:41:14,471
Just until he settles down .

477
00:41:16,141 --> 00:41:18,851
I 'm confident any inquest into this unfortunate business

478
00:41:18,935 --> 00:41:21,728
will find no connection whatsoever with Mr. Gray .

479
00:41:29,237 --> 00:41:31,446
- ( Jim roars ) - Taking you downtown .

480
00:41:33,116 --> 00:41:35,284
( Jim screams )

481
00:41:35,368 --> 00:41:37,369
( Door closes )

482
00:41:50,383 --> 00:41:52,384
This wasn 't your fault , Dorian .

483
00:41:53,970 --> 00:41:56,555
- Kelso said I was death . - Well , he was wrong .

484
00:41:56,639 --> 00:41:58,182
Salome .

485
00:41:58,266 --> 00:41:59,516
Harry ?

486
00:41:59,601 --> 00:42:01,518
You 're not making sense .

487
00:42:01,603 --> 00:42:03,103
No ! Please !

488
00:42:04,397 --> 00:42:05,606
( Scream )

489
00:42:05,690 --> 00:42:07,357
He 's part of me , Harry .

490
00:42:07,442 --> 00:42:09,735
- I turn all love into death . - Dorian . Dorian !

491
00:42:09,819 --> 00:42:11,486
Into death . Death !

492
00:42:12,530 --> 00:42:15,490
Kelso was a bitter ruin of a man and he 's dead .

493
00:42:15,575 --> 00:42:17,492
What 's past is past .

494
00:42:21,331 --> 00:42:23,498
Experience makes us strong , Dorian .

495
00:42:24,500 --> 00:42:27,002
And you need to see this episode for what it really is .

496
00:42:29,297 --> 00:42:31,298
An extraordinary experience .

497
00:42:32,842 --> 00:42:35,385
- I can 't be so heartless . - It isn 't heartless .

498
00:42:35,470 --> 00:42:37,429
It 's finding a perspective .

499
00:42:37,513 --> 00:42:40,515
Most lack the strength to rise above life 's suffering .

500
00:42:41,809 --> 00:42:43,769
To rule one 's emotions ,

501
00:42:43,853 --> 00:42:46,355
to savor them ...

502
00:42:48,441 --> 00:42:50,442
.. that takes a man of will .

503
00:42:51,361 --> 00:42:53,320
Alan left this for you .

504
00:42:54,322 --> 00:42:56,323
Drink . Doctor 's orders .

505
00:42:59,535 --> 00:43:01,536
I should be going .

506
00:43:05,959 --> 00:43:07,918
I 'll call in the morning .

507
00:43:08,962 --> 00:43:11,046
Thank you , Harry .

508
00:43:22,725 --> 00:43:25,143
You are a man of will , Dorian .

509
00:43:25,228 --> 00:43:27,229
I knew it from the first .

510
00:44:41,679 --> 00:44:42,679
( Squelching )

511
00:45:01,908 --> 00:45:03,742
Dorian , Dorian ...

512
00:45:03,826 --> 00:45:06,078
I 'm so , so sorry .

513
00:45:06,162 --> 00:45:08,580
Harry ... Harry told me about poor Sibyl .

514
00:45:08,664 --> 00:45:10,415
If there 's anything I can do ...

515
00:45:10,500 --> 00:45:13,251
You 're very kind . I 'm actually just on my way to see Harry now .

516
00:45:13,336 --> 00:45:15,796
- Are you coming to the Radleys ' ball ? - Er ...

517
00:45:18,257 --> 00:45:20,258
Where 's my picture ?

518
00:45:20,343 --> 00:45:22,803
The light was too strong in here .

519
00:45:22,887 --> 00:45:26,640
The light was perfect . Where have you put it ?

520
00:45:26,724 --> 00:45:28,683
It 's quite safe .

521
00:45:28,768 --> 00:45:31,103
The truth is , I don 't want it on public show .

522
00:45:32,063 --> 00:45:34,481
It 's just too valuable .

523
00:45:36,943 --> 00:45:40,445
I could forgive the vagaries of grief if you actually seemed to be grieving .

524
00:45:40,530 --> 00:45:42,030
I was ...

525
00:45:42,115 --> 00:45:43,448
stricken .

526
00:45:43,533 --> 00:45:45,951
But what 's past is past .

527
00:45:47,703 --> 00:45:50,372
Every experience is of value . Drink ?

528
00:45:53,584 --> 00:45:56,044
You shouldn 't believe every word Harry says .

529
00:45:57,630 --> 00:45:59,423
He doesn 't .

530
00:46:10,852 --> 00:46:14,729
Isn 't this all just ghastly ? Radley gloating with pitiful pride

531
00:46:14,814 --> 00:46:16,481
while his love-starved wife

532
00:46:16,566 --> 00:46:19,526
parades her daughter like a sow truffling for husbands .

533
00:46:19,610 --> 00:46:21,319
RADLEY : Delightful little filly .

534
00:46:21,404 --> 00:46:23,280
And poor Celia .

535
00:46:23,364 --> 00:46:27,325
Trussed up in a doily for some chinless miscreant to eternally enslave .

536
00:46:29,662 --> 00:46:31,663
I suggest we raise a little hell .

537
00:46:33,833 --> 00:46:35,917
Allow me to introduce myself .

538
00:46:36,002 --> 00:46:38,670
I know who you are , Mr. Gray .

539
00:46:38,754 --> 00:46:41,882
Allow me to offer my congratulations on your ravishing debut .

540
00:46:41,966 --> 00:46:44,176
Perhaps a small toast .

541
00:46:44,260 --> 00:46:45,969
To what ?

542
00:46:47,930 --> 00:46:49,222
Intoxication .

543
00:47:12,455 --> 00:47:14,206
- Here she comes . - Who ?

544
00:47:14,290 --> 00:47:16,291
- ( Mumbles ) - Celia ?

545
00:47:19,295 --> 00:47:21,296
- Celia ? - Problem , Lady Radley ?

546
00:47:22,673 --> 00:47:24,633
My daughter , I can 't find her .

547
00:47:24,717 --> 00:47:27,010
And nor can I find your Mr. Gray .

548
00:47:29,805 --> 00:47:33,975
Perhaps they 're in the garden . The arrangements are marvelous .

549
00:47:34,852 --> 00:47:35,810
Ah .

550
00:47:35,895 --> 00:47:38,230
Might I hazard an alternative suggestion ?

551
00:47:42,026 --> 00:47:44,319
Waltz

552
00:47:49,534 --> 00:47:51,159
( Hums waltz )

553
00:47:58,292 --> 00:47:59,918
Celia !

554
00:48:00,002 --> 00:48:02,420
- Is something the matter ? - Celia !

555
00:48:06,133 --> 00:48:08,593
Where is my daughter , you beast ?

556
00:48:08,678 --> 00:48:11,221
I was just attending to my costume .

557
00:48:11,305 --> 00:48:16,309
A little of Lord Radley 's very fine Burgundy was spilt on my shirt cuff .

558
00:48:19,188 --> 00:48:21,523
Oh . Oh ...

559
00:48:22,525 --> 00:48:24,401
Mr. Gray , I ...

560
00:48:24,485 --> 00:48:27,487
- Lord Henry gave me to understand ... - A mistake .

561
00:48:27,572 --> 00:48:30,115
Nobody at all need know .

562
00:48:33,244 --> 00:48:35,704
You 're too kind , Mr. Gray .

563
00:48:37,206 --> 00:48:39,624
- Thank you . - It must be difficult ,

564
00:48:39,709 --> 00:48:41,710
a party like this .

565
00:48:42,712 --> 00:48:44,713
Seeing your daughter come of age .

566
00:48:46,465 --> 00:48:48,675
Makes you long for your own youth .

567
00:48:51,512 --> 00:48:53,096
I ...

568
00:48:53,180 --> 00:48:55,140
Madam , forgive me but ...

569
00:48:57,226 --> 00:48:59,728
.. you are exquisite .

570
00:49:02,023 --> 00:49:03,940
Oh , Mr. Gray .

571
00:49:04,025 --> 00:49:06,526
This is most improper . ( Gasps )

572
00:49:08,571 --> 00:49:09,904
Ooh ...

573
00:49:11,365 --> 00:49:12,574
Ah !

574
00:49:18,914 --> 00:49:19,914
Oh !

575
00:49:55,785 --> 00:49:57,702
Now , where were we ?

576
00:49:57,787 --> 00:49:59,704
( Applause )

577
00:49:59,789 --> 00:50:01,873
What are you grinning about , Gray ?

578
00:50:02,833 --> 00:50:04,918
I think Harry 's just lost a wager .

579
00:50:05,002 --> 00:50:08,421
Well , come on , out with it . We 're all gambling men here .

580
00:50:08,506 --> 00:50:10,590
Just a little round of double or nothing .

581
00:50:10,675 --> 00:50:12,175
( Laughs )

582
00:50:12,259 --> 00:50:16,012
Of course , a good gambler understands that there are limits .

583
00:50:16,097 --> 00:50:18,223
BOTH : There are no limits .

584
00:50:32,780 --> 00:50:34,489
( Thunder )

585
00:51:01,267 --> 00:51:03,810
( Operatic singing in Italian )

586
00:51:15,823 --> 00:51:17,824
Have a wonderful birthday , Dorian !

587
00:51:27,251 --> 00:51:29,002
( Laughs ) Dorian .

588
00:51:29,086 --> 00:51:31,796
This crush is your finest yet .

589
00:51:31,881 --> 00:51:35,216
One has to do something to null the pain of age .

590
00:51:35,301 --> 00:51:37,469
Do tell my husband not to be so disagreeable .

591
00:51:37,553 --> 00:51:39,554
But I always agree with him .

592
00:51:40,556 --> 00:51:43,433
Congratulations , Basil . I hear you have a new exhibition .

593
00:51:43,517 --> 00:51:45,435
Yes , yes , in Paris .

594
00:51:45,519 --> 00:51:48,229
Yes , in fact , I wanted to ask a question of you , Dorian .

595
00:51:48,230 --> 00:51:50,815
I 'd like to make your portrait my principal piece .

596
00:51:50,900 --> 00:51:55,236
Oh , yes , that picture . Absolutely wonderful .

597
00:51:55,321 --> 00:51:59,115
- Whatever became of it ? - I haven 't seen it myself in months .

598
00:51:59,200 --> 00:52:01,910
- He 's very protective of it , aren 't you ? - Indeed I am .

599
00:52:01,994 --> 00:52:04,704
I 'm very sorry , Basil , but it 's just too precious .

600
00:52:06,499 --> 00:52:08,750
I won 't have it out of the house .

601
00:52:18,761 --> 00:52:20,762
( Moans of pleasure )

602
00:52:28,729 --> 00:52:31,272
I beg your pardon .

603
00:52:31,357 --> 00:52:33,274
Did you want me ?

604
00:52:35,736 --> 00:52:39,989
That picture is my finest work and it 'd be greatly appreciated ...

605
00:52:40,074 --> 00:52:42,909
The greatest gift that anyone could ever have given .

606
00:52:43,786 --> 00:52:45,203
In fact ...

607
00:52:46,789 --> 00:52:50,041
In fact , I wish that I could tell you just how great .

608
00:52:51,544 --> 00:52:55,588
But then it isn 't so unreasonable to borrow it back a little while .

609
00:52:57,216 --> 00:52:59,217
I 'm not sure that I 've ever ...

610
00:52:59,969 --> 00:53:02,512
.. fully expressed my gratitude .

611
00:53:05,391 --> 00:53:07,183
I hardly think ...

612
00:53:43,262 --> 00:53:45,263
( African drumbeat )

613
00:54:31,143 --> 00:54:33,144
I have the key to your heart .

614
00:54:35,689 --> 00:54:38,566
Don 't touch that ever !

615
00:54:38,651 --> 00:54:39,734
Dorian !

616
00:54:45,240 --> 00:54:47,033
He 's young .

617
00:54:47,117 --> 00:54:49,077
But he was never cruel

618
00:54:49,161 --> 00:54:51,454
till he met you .

619
00:54:54,959 --> 00:54:56,918
That 's mine .

620
00:55:06,512 --> 00:55:08,429
( Drumbeat intensifies )

621
00:55:18,107 --> 00:55:20,024
( Knocking )

622
00:55:20,109 --> 00:55:22,777
- ( Door opens ) DORIAN : Oh , it 's you .

623
00:55:25,906 --> 00:55:28,658
- I thought you 'd gone home . - I just needed a walk .

624
00:55:28,742 --> 00:55:31,619
I was just about to go to bed . Everyone 's left .

625
00:55:31,704 --> 00:55:33,705
I 'm here to see you , not them .

626
00:55:34,790 --> 00:55:36,207
Really ?

627
00:55:41,380 --> 00:55:43,381
Wait , wait .

628
00:55:46,969 --> 00:55:48,886
I don 't know where to begin .

629
00:55:48,971 --> 00:55:51,180
How ominous .

630
00:55:54,518 --> 00:55:57,645
- You terrified that poor boy tonight . - He seemed to recover .

631
00:55:57,730 --> 00:56:00,732
Is that what you tell yourself about Celia Radley ?

632
00:56:00,816 --> 00:56:03,818
Look , I 'm sorry about her misfortune .

633
00:56:03,902 --> 00:56:05,945
But do you really believe that I 'm to blame ?

634
00:56:10,993 --> 00:56:13,995
When I look at you , I find it impossible to imagine .

635
00:56:15,330 --> 00:56:18,082
But I know you 're treating people poorly .

636
00:56:18,167 --> 00:56:19,709
Even me ,

637
00:56:19,793 --> 00:56:23,671
when I ask you the small favor that you loan me my own picture ...

638
00:56:23,756 --> 00:56:26,758
- Is that what this is about ? - No , it 's about a good deal more !

639
00:56:37,019 --> 00:56:38,519
Dorian ...

640
00:57:00,000 --> 00:57:03,336
What happened to the Dorian Gray I painted ?

641
00:57:03,420 --> 00:57:05,630
You just don 't understand .

642
00:57:10,636 --> 00:57:12,386
I will always ...

643
00:57:12,471 --> 00:57:14,597
be that Dorian .

644
00:57:17,976 --> 00:57:20,186
Can I trust you , Basil ?

645
00:57:22,648 --> 00:57:26,400
Would you like to see why you can never exhibit that picture ?

646
00:57:47,339 --> 00:57:49,340
What 's the matter ?

647
00:57:50,425 --> 00:57:52,385
Don 't you recognize me ?

648
00:57:52,469 --> 00:57:54,470
What have you ... ?

649
00:57:55,347 --> 00:57:57,181
That thing ...

650
00:57:57,266 --> 00:57:59,433
It isn 't what ...

651
00:57:59,434 --> 00:58:02,186
Together , we 've created something beautiful .

652
00:58:06,233 --> 00:58:08,234
It 's a miracle .

653
00:58:12,698 --> 00:58:14,699
Look at me .

654
00:58:16,034 --> 00:58:17,785
Look at me .

655
00:58:19,496 --> 00:58:21,497
Because of your painting ...

656
00:58:22,666 --> 00:58:26,210
- It 's not ... - .. this will never age .

657
00:58:26,295 --> 00:58:28,546
Will never scar .

658
00:58:33,719 --> 00:58:35,595
Can you even imagine

659
00:58:35,679 --> 00:58:38,222
being able to do anything you please ...

660
00:58:40,475 --> 00:58:42,727
.. and live out every whim and impulse

661
00:58:42,811 --> 00:58:45,396
while the world just sees you gleam ?

662
00:58:45,480 --> 00:58:47,231
This isn 't you .

663
00:58:47,316 --> 00:58:49,692
I know this isn 't you . We can stop it !

664
00:58:49,776 --> 00:58:52,069
Basil , please , don 't .

665
00:58:52,154 --> 00:58:55,448
Don 't you see that this must be destroyed ?

666
00:58:55,532 --> 00:58:57,491
Dorian , I want to help you .

667
00:58:57,576 --> 00:59:00,953
We 'll find a priest or a spirit-worker .

668
00:59:01,038 --> 00:59:02,914
( Scrape of broken glass )

669
00:59:02,998 --> 00:59:05,750
There 's good in your heart . I 've seen it .

670
00:59:05,834 --> 00:59:08,085
You 're not this ...

671
00:59:08,170 --> 00:59:09,921
this devil !

672
00:59:14,092 --> 00:59:15,927
I 'm a god .

673
00:59:17,512 --> 00:59:18,846
Basil .

674
00:59:19,598 --> 00:59:20,932
Basil !

675
00:59:35,030 --> 00:59:37,073
( Basil chokes )

676
00:59:44,748 --> 00:59:46,791
( Basil moans gently )

677
01:00:14,987 --> 01:00:17,655
( Flutter of wings )

678
01:00:26,999 --> 01:00:29,000
( Echo of howling wind )

679
01:01:05,037 --> 01:01:07,038
( Sniffs )

680
01:01:11,460 --> 01:01:12,960
( Exhales )

681
01:01:25,682 --> 01:01:26,932
( Gasps )

682
01:01:27,017 --> 01:01:29,018
( Thunder )

683
01:01:42,574 --> 01:01:44,283
Good evening .

684
01:01:47,371 --> 01:01:49,372
Need some help , sir ?

685
01:01:53,418 --> 01:01:55,086
How kind .

686
01:01:55,087 --> 01:01:57,129
( Rattling thud )

687
01:01:59,424 --> 01:02:00,633
All right .

688
01:02:06,640 --> 01:02:08,557
Mind how you go , sir .

689
01:02:08,642 --> 01:02:10,559
On you go .

690
01:02:15,190 --> 01:02:16,440
( Ship 's horn )

691
01:02:16,441 --> 01:02:16,857
( Ship 's horn )

692
01:02:18,193 --> 01:02:20,194
( Clanking and grinding )

693
01:03:37,939 --> 01:03:39,940
( Woman screams )

694
01:03:50,827 --> 01:03:53,412
( Moans of ecstasy )

695
01:03:59,920 --> 01:04:01,921
( Rasping gasp )

696
01:04:05,842 --> 01:04:08,677
( Rasping sigh )

697
01:04:14,142 --> 01:04:16,060
Good day , Lady Victoria .

698
01:04:16,895 --> 01:04:20,773
I was about to take Harry for lunch at Scott 's . Why don 't you join us ?

699
01:04:21,775 --> 01:04:24,944
Oh , Dorian . You haven 't heard .

700
01:04:26,863 --> 01:04:30,115
They 've found Basil 's body in the river .

701
01:04:36,206 --> 01:04:38,040
Thou art slave to Fate ,

702
01:04:38,124 --> 01:04:41,544
Chance , kings and desperate men ,

703
01:04:42,796 --> 01:04:46,006
And dost with poyson , warre and sicknesse dwell ,

704
01:04:47,133 --> 01:04:50,427
And poppies or charmes can make us sleepe as well ,

705
01:04:50,512 --> 01:04:52,513
And better than thy stroake .

706
01:04:53,723 --> 01:04:55,724
Why swell 'st thou then ?

707
01:04:57,477 --> 01:04:59,895
One short sleepe past ,

708
01:04:59,980 --> 01:05:01,981
we wake eternally .

709
01:05:03,233 --> 01:05:05,609
And death shall be no more .

710
01:05:08,446 --> 01:05:11,240
Death , thou shalt die .

711
01:05:29,426 --> 01:05:32,469
Farewell , dear Basil .

712
01:05:35,015 --> 01:05:37,182
DORIAN : I spoke to the police again this morning .

713
01:05:37,267 --> 01:05:40,603
And have the buffoons managed to make a single inch of progress ?

714
01:05:40,687 --> 01:05:43,063
They 're convinced it was some Shadwell renter .

715
01:05:43,148 --> 01:05:45,107
They think they 'll catch him .

716
01:05:45,191 --> 01:05:48,152
So Basil 's name will be dragged through the gutter .

717
01:05:50,822 --> 01:05:52,823
I 'm of a mind to take a trip , Harry .

718
01:05:54,451 --> 01:05:56,410
Maybe you should join me .

719
01:05:56,494 --> 01:05:58,787
- Where are you going ? - Everywhere .

720
01:05:58,872 --> 01:06:00,998
I leave tomorrow .

721
01:06:01,082 --> 01:06:02,499
With all this ?

722
01:06:04,002 --> 01:06:06,962
Someone once gave me some fine advice ...

723
01:06:08,214 --> 01:06:10,633
.. about taking perspective .

724
01:06:10,717 --> 01:06:12,551
Come with me .

725
01:06:17,390 --> 01:06:19,933
The child is imminent .

726
01:06:21,686 --> 01:06:23,687
Tell me everything .

727
01:06:27,651 --> 01:06:29,443
I always do .

728
01:06:56,262 --> 01:06:59,473
DORIAN : I 've entered the tombs of dead nations ,

729
01:06:59,557 --> 01:07:02,518
ridden with our last savage tribes .

730
01:07:02,602 --> 01:07:04,436
I feel the brilliance of every moment ,

731
01:07:04,521 --> 01:07:06,772
the splendor of existence and its awful ...

732
01:07:06,856 --> 01:07:11,568
.. keen as the edge of a blade , this desperate will to see , touch and ...

733
01:07:11,653 --> 01:07:16,073
Dearest Harry , you taught me that life must burn with a hard flame .

734
01:07:16,157 --> 01:07:18,242
Its light does not blind me ,

735
01:07:18,326 --> 01:07:20,202
nor its heat sear me .

736
01:07:20,286 --> 01:07:22,204
I am the flame , Harry .

737
01:07:22,288 --> 01:07:24,373
I am the flame .

738
01:08:20,555 --> 01:08:23,015
( Rasping gasp )

739
01:08:23,099 --> 01:08:24,641
( Gramophone crackles )

740
01:08:24,726 --> 01:08:28,187
HENRY : Women never have anything to say , but they say it charmingly .

741
01:08:28,271 --> 01:08:30,773
They 're the great triumph of matter over mind .

742
01:08:30,857 --> 01:08:32,858
( Laughter )

743
01:08:33,902 --> 01:08:35,569
Well , here I am .

744
01:09:08,311 --> 01:09:09,686
Dorian .

745
01:09:10,522 --> 01:09:12,523
You look so ...

746
01:09:13,691 --> 01:09:15,025
.. so ...

747
01:09:17,445 --> 01:09:19,446
( Whispering )

748
01:09:22,200 --> 01:09:24,201
He looks magnificent .

749
01:09:25,537 --> 01:09:29,581
We have heard such tales .

750
01:09:30,750 --> 01:09:34,795
I 'm afraid they 're all absolutely and entirely ... true .

751
01:09:34,879 --> 01:09:36,213
( Murmuring )

752
01:09:39,259 --> 01:09:41,009
Welcome back .

753
01:09:41,094 --> 01:09:43,095
Some champagne ?

754
01:09:43,930 --> 01:09:45,722
Yes .

755
01:09:50,770 --> 01:09:52,145
A-ha !

756
01:09:52,230 --> 01:09:54,231
My missing guest of honor .

757
01:09:56,651 --> 01:09:58,443
I 'm coming .

758
01:10:06,411 --> 01:10:08,412
I was sorry for your loss .

759
01:10:14,085 --> 01:10:16,295
You know , I kept hearing this phrase .

760
01:10:17,881 --> 01:10:19,882
" Natural causes . "

761
01:10:22,302 --> 01:10:24,428
Nature has a great deal to answer for .

762
01:10:25,430 --> 01:10:28,307
She was so looking forward to the life of a divorcee .

763
01:10:29,309 --> 01:10:30,976
And poor old Basil ...

764
01:10:32,270 --> 01:10:36,148
If we paid the police by results , we 'd save the Treasury thousands .

765
01:10:37,817 --> 01:10:40,277
When your letters stopped coming , I feared the worst .

766
01:10:40,361 --> 01:10:42,362
But here you are .

767
01:10:44,198 --> 01:10:46,366
So never mind the country estate .

768
01:10:46,451 --> 01:10:49,620
Tell me , why are you really back ?

769
01:10:51,039 --> 01:10:54,333
- I 'm tired . - You don 't look it .

770
01:10:54,417 --> 01:10:56,460
You have no right to melancholy .

771
01:10:56,544 --> 01:10:58,378
Your life is exquisite .

772
01:10:58,463 --> 01:11:02,257
You 've drunk deeply of everything and it hasn 't left a fleck on you .

773
01:11:03,384 --> 01:11:06,428
Do you remember when I first came to London ?

774
01:11:09,724 --> 01:11:11,558
I felt so ...

775
01:11:11,643 --> 01:11:14,394
Those were the great days .

776
01:11:14,479 --> 01:11:18,482
Dorian , it 's quite clear why you 've lost your passion for life .

777
01:11:19,567 --> 01:11:22,736
You 've been away from me for too long .

778
01:11:22,820 --> 01:11:25,072
We must go out .

779
01:11:25,156 --> 01:11:27,157
Take on the town , as we used to .

780
01:11:32,664 --> 01:11:36,041
- I 've missed you , Harry . - I must ask you , though ...

781
01:11:39,963 --> 01:11:41,755
What is your secret ?

782
01:11:42,924 --> 01:11:46,468
If I told you , I 'd have to kill you .

783
01:11:48,763 --> 01:11:50,764
You still have it , I see .

784
01:11:52,350 --> 01:11:54,810
- From Cairo . - Where else ?

785
01:12:02,986 --> 01:12:04,528
Smile .

786
01:12:08,992 --> 01:12:10,409
Emily .

787
01:12:11,911 --> 01:12:14,162
May I ?

788
01:12:16,082 --> 01:12:18,834
I hope I 'm not interrupting your reminiscence ?

789
01:12:18,918 --> 01:12:21,753
The one charm of the past is that it 's the past .

790
01:12:21,838 --> 01:12:25,924
Oh . I hope you 're not also a dreary old cynic ?

791
01:12:26,009 --> 01:12:27,801
What is there to believe in ?

792
01:12:29,554 --> 01:12:32,014
Our developments .

793
01:12:33,057 --> 01:12:34,933
All I see is decay .

794
01:12:36,060 --> 01:12:37,519
Well , religion ?

795
01:12:37,603 --> 01:12:40,022
Fashionable substitute for belief .

796
01:12:40,106 --> 01:12:42,107
- Art ? - A malady .

797
01:12:42,191 --> 01:12:44,026
